## Vercel Web Analytics Installation Complete

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js project following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart.

### Changes Made

**Modified Files:**
1. `app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics component to the root layout
   - Imported `Analytics` from `@vercel/analytics/next`
   - Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag, after `<SitePageShell>`
   - Follows the Next.js App Router pattern as per official documentation

2. `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
   - Added `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 to dependencies

3. `pnpm-lock.yaml` - Updated lockfile
   - Added all necessary dependencies for @vercel/analytics package

### Implementation Details

This project uses Next.js 16.1.6 with the App Router pattern. Following the official Vercel documentation, I:

1. Installed the `@vercel/analytics` package using pnpm (the project's package manager)
2. Imported the Analytics component from `@vercel/analytics/next` in the root layout
3. Placed the `<Analytics />` component at the end of the `<body>` tag for optimal performance

The Analytics component is now set up and will automatically track page views and Web Vitals once the project is deployed to Vercel.

### Verification

✅ Build successful - No compilation errors
✅ Linting passed - No ESLint errors
✅ Dependencies installed - pnpm-lock.yaml updated correctly

### Next Steps

To complete the setup:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in your Vercel dashboard under the Analytics tab
3. View analytics data after users visit your site

No additional configuration is required. The Analytics component will automatically detect the Vercel environment and begin collecting data.
